# Hint text

Place a short piece of help where it supports the answer.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use a hint to explain a unit, expected format or consequence that most people need before answering. An option can have its own hint when the label alone is insufficient.

## When not to use it

Do not put a long manual, links, details controls or essential safety instructions inside a hint. A placeholder is not a substitute because it disappears while typing.

## Home Assistant adaptation

For Home Assistant, explain human concepts rather than internal entity or service names unless an advanced configuration task requires those identifiers. State whether a value changes only the display or affects an automation. Keep extended help in normal page content outside the described-by text.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Place the hint after the label or legend and before the field. Connect it using aria-describedby. Keep additional error IDs in that association when validation fails. Short hints reduce repetitive screen-reader output.

## Examples

### Explain a recognisable display name

The hint helps people choose a label without exposing implementation details.

<%= example('nhs-hint-name') %>

### Clarify what a setting affects

The saved display preference is distinct from the recorded measurement.

<%= example('nhs-hint-scope') %>

## Check the implementation

Test the field with its label, hint and error announced together. Check that guidance remains visible at increased text size and does not rely on colour or position.

Use the [civica accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS hint text](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/hint-text) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica markup, Arial typography and civica assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

